Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='markednothidden', at=datetime(2026, 9, 2, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='Agent content is marked (unconfirmed), not hidden; confirmation is a trusted re-append, human-only', body='*Agent content is MARKED, not hidden* (2026-09-02). The content register folds `Authored` from every actor (a fold that dropped them would be an outage reporting success), so the trust asymmetry is carried to the reader: every generated block carries `authoredBy:` (and `state:`/`resolvedAt:` from the trusted fold), typst reads nothing on the side (no projection file), and every reader (the web app, `suzatary todos open`) tags a triage-authored todo `(unconfirmed)` where it stands — never moved or sunk, because a mis-priced provisional todo hidden at the bottom is the failure the marker prevents. Confirmation is a trusted re-append of the same content: `suzatary todo confirm <id>`, human-only like sending, no MCP twin (test-pinned; an agent that can confirm itself has confirmed nothing). The provisional record stays on the chain.', rationale='Decided 2026-09-02.', supersedes=()))